<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia Jan-July trade deficit widens.</title>
<headline>Slovakia Jan-July trade deficit widens.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak Foreign trade deficit for the first seven months of the year widened to 31.895 billion crowns, from 26.97 billion for the January-June period, the Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>SLOVAK FOREIGN TRADE  Jan-July '96  Jan-June '96  Jan-July '95</p>
<p> exports (SKK bln)	150.236	 127.59	  144.515</p>
<p> imports		    182.131	 154.56	  144.341</p>
<p> balance		    -31.895	 -26.97	   +0.174</p>
<p>Note. All figures, which are calculated on a custom-cleared basis, are preliminary and subject to revision. SUSR said it expects to issue final 1995 figures by the end of the third quarter.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
